note Parse before indexing so a usage error costs nothing. Then build the index and run every pending language server to completion, so the answer is from the server whenever one is on PATH. Help goes to stdout with exit 0, usage errors to stderr with exit 2. A map that does not read stops the command with exit 2, before anything could save over it. A mutating command saves the map. A command error prints what it produced so far and exits 2; check relies on this. Output goes through emit so a closed pipe does not panic.

